      "description": "Marion A. Zioncheck (also Marion Zioncheck, Marion Anthony Zioncheck) was a U.S. Representative / Seattle congressman (1933–1936). Official reports said he died by suicide at the Arctic Building in Seattle on 7 August 1936. He Didn't Jump publishes newspapers and five volumes that re-examine that official account.",
